{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"feedback feedback","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback.md","fileName":"Feedback.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Feedback","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Human-Computer Interaction Foundations]] [[Game Interactivity]] [[Player Experience Layers]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human-Computer Interaction Foundations","Game Interactivity","Player Experience Layers","User-System Loop","Conceptual Model","Feedback Compliance","Game-Player System","Player Mental Model","Engagement","Robust Game Verb","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf","gamesdesignandplay.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"feedback feedback","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback.md","fileName":"Feedback.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Feedback","heading":"Feedback","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Feedback is information that helps a user understand system state, the result of an operation, or progress on a task. It can come from the system, the environment, or the user's own body.\n\nSensory feedback may be visual, auditory, haptic, chemical, proprioceptive, or kinesthetic. Reactive feedback comes from operating the interface, instrumental feedback comes from controls and tools, and operational feedback communicates the system's result.\n\nUseful feedback closes the [[User-System Loop]] and supports an accurate [[Conceptual Model]]. Multiple channels can reinforce one another, but they should maintain [[Feedback Compliance]] in space and time.\n\nIn a [[Game-Player System]], feedback is also the return path by which the result of a player's action changes the [[Player Mental Model]]. A behavior should provide timely, comprehensible evidence of relevant state change; missing or inexplicable feedback prevents the player from testing predictions and weakens [[Engagement]].\n\nA [[Robust Game Verb]] provides feedback even when an action is refused. A sound, animation, or other visible reaction can teach why an object resists the verb instead of leaving the player uncertain whether the input was received.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human-Computer Interaction Foundations","Game Interactivity","Player Experience Layers","User-System Loop","Conceptual Model","Feedback Compliance","Game-Player System","Player Mental Model","Engagement","Robust Game Verb","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf","gamesdesignandplay.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"feedback feedback","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback.md","fileName":"Feedback.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Feedback","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf]]\n[[advancedgamedesign.pdf]]\n[[agamedesignvocabulary.pdf]]\n[[gamesdesignandplay.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Human-Computer Interaction Foundations","Game Interactivity","Player Experience Layers","User-System Loop","Conceptual Model","Feedback Compliance","Game-Player System","Player Mental Model","Engagement","Robust Game Verb","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agamedesignvocabulary.pdf","gamesdesignandplay.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}